/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  componentLookup01_catalogue_ladder
  ==================================

  WHAT IT IS.  "Does Choupo have this compound, and what does its record
  carry?" as ONE operation with a fixed byte budget (2048 bytes) and the same
  evidence-card format as pairLookup (DEV.md 4c C227, slice a).  The query
  resolves by RECORD -- a catalogue file name, a declared alias or a CAS --
  never by name similarity.  Four operations:

      c_name   ethanol          the catalogue record, by name
      c_cas    64-17-5          the SAME record, by CAS
      c_lake   1Pentadecanol    only in the group-estimate lake: identity and
                                UNIFAC groups, NO values, "not reviewed"
      c_none   unobtainium      "I do not have this compound"

  The card lists which properties the record has and which it lacks; it never
  prints the values (they are in the record, and a case uses the name).
  Pinned: the tier word of each card and its byte count.  The
  thermoPhysPropDict is a placeholder the bench requires; no op reads it.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
operations
(
    { name c_name; type componentLookup; component ethanol; }
    { name c_cas;  type componentLookup; component 64-17-5; }
    { name c_lake; type componentLookup; component 1Pentadecanol; }
    { name c_none; type componentLookup; component unobtainium; }
);
